{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_37104d1129062a232a57c7f1f11cebc15b81f698e1cc3b9190afb4f21fdce60b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"All commands output TOON, a compact JSON encoding optimized for LLM token usage, by default; passing --json yields standard JSON."},{"claim_ids":["clm_45d5e65643661d3da840a80567cccfb9c8273c0f6c35adcfb3ea2564d1e12d45"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"dora requires a SCIP indexer for its language; scip-typescript is shown for TypeScript/JavaScript, with pointers to scip-java, rust-analyzer, scip-python, scip-ruby, scip-clang, scip-dotnet, and scip-dart for other languages."},{"claim_ids":["clm_513c84712bc0f64731b3d55104fc2792c1b66a2c56beb489c67af108bd8167c7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the root README points contributors to CONTRIBUTING.md for contribution guidance."},{"claim_ids":["clm_760156e21eee44caf72ee36d291528f44b65817e153f285d4355db1979ee54bb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"dora mcp starts an MCP server over stdio, and the README shows registering it with Claude Code via 'claude mcp add --transport stdio dora -- dora mcp'."},{"claim_ids":["clm_885f600a74850f1b837bec893cf6d63953483884f6b797d056f681636bb0ceac"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"dora init creates a .dora directory containing config.json (indexer command, ignore patterns, grammar paths), index.scip (raw SCIP protobuf), and dora.db, the SQLite database dora queries."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8d557d7446b3445b1ad5bb33ee5eb7c151a6c45743052d9ed9b3abbb94b72335"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Besides prebuilt binaries for macOS ARM, macOS Intel, and Linux x64, dora can be installed via npm using Bun ('bun install -g @butttons/dora')."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8e919bf4b9d9b9ea868e5d50e32d0d09af50c686a99106ea5dde81f9ab303a42"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"dora is a CLI that turns a SCIP index into a queryable SQLite database, giving AI agents structured answers about a codebase instead of grepping files and reading imports."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9d28b22943393267a15dc812adabd93cf55e44a24e944f47405e9a0b0ffca1b9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool has two layers: a SCIP layer that runs a configured indexer, parses the resulting protobuf, and loads symbols, references, and file dependencies into SQLite; and a tree-sitter layer that parses source on demand via WebAssembly grammars for things SCIP doesn't cover."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d5f4a228921bdc03131df538603c408e5c964166680773112d9fe9fefa45e76c"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Tree-sitter analysis commands need a grammar installed, e.g. 'bun add -g tree-sitter-typescript' for TypeScript/JavaScript."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fdae466263ac23313f2e20b0c854cacdb6f206eff1a5bab5d3c94bd4c3887ef0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The SQLite schema stores denormalized counts (symbol_count, dependency_count, dependent_count, reference_count) so most queries are index lookups rather than aggregations."}],"claim_ids":["clm_37104d1129062a232a57c7f1f11cebc15b81f698e1cc3b9190afb4f21fdce60b","clm_45d5e65643661d3da840a80567cccfb9c8273c0f6c35adcfb3ea2564d1e12d45","clm_513c84712bc0f64731b3d55104fc2792c1b66a2c56beb489c67af108bd8167c7","clm_760156e21eee44caf72ee36d291528f44b65817e153f285d4355db1979ee54bb","clm_885f600a74850f1b837bec893cf6d63953483884f6b797d056f681636bb0ceac","clm_8d557d7446b3445b1ad5bb33ee5eb7c151a6c45743052d9ed9b3abbb94b72335","clm_8e919bf4b9d9b9ea868e5d50e32d0d09af50c686a99106ea5dde81f9ab303a42","clm_9d28b22943393267a15dc812adabd93cf55e44a24e944f47405e9a0b0ffca1b9","clm_d5f4a228921bdc03131df538603c408e5c964166680773112d9fe9fefa45e76c","clm_fdae466263ac23313f2e20b0c854cacdb6f206eff1a5bab5d3c94bd4c3887ef0"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:39:38Z","created_by_operation":"op_162cafdec75f4d0ba4c9e50992162cff","id":"pg_10d769f14dca59c79fe6b9aeb6556938","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/butttons-dora-readme-md-f4edb8fd349e-b9aeb6556938.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_versio